# Line-ending rules for the packaging tree.
# PowerShell scripts must keep LF endings in every checkout: a
# backtick continuation followed by CRLF breaks the PowerShell parser
# (the backtick escapes the CR, not the LF). The runtime scripts also
# avoid backtick continuations entirely; this is the second lock.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.iss text eol=lf
# Batch files are safest with native Windows endings.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
